% =============================================================================
%  BIBLIOGRAPHY — v3 ENTRIES ONLY
% -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
%  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, AND WHY v3 NEVER ADDS TO bibliography.bib
%
%  bibliography.bib is INHERITED from v2 byte-for-byte, exactly like
%  parts/00_preamble.tex. That is what lets a v2 bibliography change
%  fast-forward into v3 with no conflict and no merge. The moment v3 appends an
%  entry to that file, every future v2 bibliography pass becomes a three-way
%  merge on a file where both sides append at the end — the worst possible
%  conflict shape, and one that recurs on every single pass.
%
%  So: v2 owns bibliography.bib. v3 owns this file. Neither ever writes the
%  other's. biblatex merges them at build time; \addbibresource is additive and
%  duplicate keys across resources are reported by biber, so a key that lands in
%  BOTH files is caught at build rather than silently shadowed.
%
%  Which v2 revision the inherited bibliography.bib came from is recorded in
%  inherited/SYNC_STATE.json (field `v2_version`), stamped by tools/sync_v2.py.
%
%  IF A v3 ENTRY BELONGS IN BOTH DRAFTS: add it to ../v2/bibliography.bib and
%  run `python3 tools/sync_v2.py merge` to pull it down. Never the other way —
%  see inherited/MANIFEST.md, "The one-way rule".
%
%  SOURCING RULE, inherited from v2 unchanged: an entry is either verified
%  against a PDF in /workspaces/aux_repo/PAPERS/ (then it carries `file = {...}`
%  relative to that root, and title/authors/year were read off that copy's own
%  title page), or it is marked `% NO LOCAL COPY` and is UNVERIFIED. Never write
%  an entry from memory: v2's first α-Flow entry was written that way and was
%  wrong in the title and in every author.
% =============================================================================

